A||N||10||Monkeyman||Changing the battery tray??||||1||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||04-26-2000||09:38 AM||||The battery tray/box in the Grape Ape is rusted pretty badly.  What can I do to change it?  I was going to swap parts with the Monkeymobile, but it looks like that one is welded in place.  Any suggestions???||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fret Naught||04-26-2000||09:52 AM||||I had the same problem, pay close attention to the fuel line fittings located close to the tray, mine were getting coroaded. I measured and built a tray, and used sheet metal screws to attach it on three sides. It is working good. but I planned on this being a temp. fix. I see that the Fiero Store has replacement trays that can be welded or rivited into place. That is route I am going to go. I don't have a heat shield on my fix. I think it is probably a good idea to have one. When I do the permenant fix it will include a heat shield.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||04-26-2000||02:04 PM||||My try is gone altogether and the battery is being held with a piece of wood (which is bad, because if it slips a millimeter, it ends up in the pulley).. Does anyone know of an aftermarket holder that will fit it in there nicely? I would get straps, but can't think of anywhere to attach them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan||04-26-2000||02:33 PM|||| At last check,  the battery tray was still available at the Dealership.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||04-26-2000||02:42 PM||||Be <B>extremely</B> careful if you weld the tray! you have to remove the seats, rear carpet, and insulation unless you want to start a fire!  see link below <A HREF="http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/parks/electric.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/parks/electric.htm</A> ||||reg||4
Z||000005||peterh||04-26-2000||03:12 PM||||I agree that you should not try welding a new tray in due to danger of fire. I got the Fiero store battery tray and hold-down and pop riveted them in. Works great.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||04-26-2000||03:38 PM||||I can't weld nor do I have access to a welder.  I planned on either pop riveting it in or using screws.  How do I get the old one out?  Will a cut off disc on a Dremel be enough to cut off the old one?  I checked out the Fiero Store.  They have different parts for the battery tray.  Which parts do I need?  Would it help if I posted a pic of what my car looks like now?||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfixit58||04-26-2000||04:27 PM||||Move the battery up front.<P>If you can get to them with a drill, you can buy a spot weld removal bit from Eastwood. It works great. I used one on my 69 Firebird.<P>Roy||||reg||1
Z||000008||Mark||04-26-2000||07:18 PM||||Yes you can cut the old tray out with a Dremmel tool and cutoff disk, just be patient.  Also, the replacement tray and support bracket are still available from the dealers (both pieces) for about $25 or less.  And yes, you can pop rivet the new tray in place.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Gokart||04-26-2000||08:49 PM||||Got lucky when I bought my parts car when I found a brand new battery tray in the trunk! Must have been a future project that never happened. I didn't have a dremmel when I removed my old rusted one so I used my sawzail and a pair of vice grips bending loose pieces back and forth till I got it all out. Had to scribe marks for bolts and drilled them out and 20 minutes later new battery tray! I want to put the battery up front this summer but heard many dissatisfied people with V8-Archies kit. Anyone know of another? One that's NOT made of metal?||||reg||1
Z||000010||BOILERMAKER||04-27-2000||12:27 AM||||When I replaced my old one we ended up using a pneumatic chisel (the ones that sound like hammer, but vibrate and cut like a chisel).  We put the replacement back in the original place using screws and silicon to fill in the cuts left by the chisel (hey, nobody is perfect ... and you can't even tell).<P>BTW, I have an extra one that the fiero store sent me by accident (I paid for the wrong part apparently and haven't sent it back yet) if you need it.  I'll sell it to you for cost.||||reg||1
